      {
        "sha": "6ad985f1e58e5d6d281c80c962e96200dcac25c6",
        "node_id": "C_kwDOBSIeiNoAKDZhZDk4NWYxZTU4ZTVkNmQyODFjODBjOTYyZTk2MjAwZGNhYzI1YzY",
        "commit": {
          "author": {
            "name": "William McDonald",
            "email": "william.mcdonald@discordapp.com",
            "date": "2023-04-12T07:12:52Z"
          },
          "committer": {
            "name": "William McDonald",
            "email": "william.mcdonald@discordapp.com",
            "date": "2023-04-12T19:55:33Z"
          },
          "message": "[lilliput] Add jpeg content length detection\n\nWalk jpeg segments to find EOI and report content length accurately\nSadly this seems to require a linear scan of the content\n\na jpeg file consists of a sequence of segments\n- segments are delimited by 0xFF, then a single non-zero byte for type\n- EOI segment type is is 0xD9 while SOI is 0xD8\n- most segments have 2 bytes for size following the type, but not the\n  actual image data in entropy coded segments (ECS)\n- ECS is not delimited by 0xFF\n- in ECS, 0xFF may occur naturally and is marked as data instead of a\n  new segment by adding 0x00 immediately after the 0xFF\n\nAdd a couple unit tests for jpeg data",
          "tree": {
            "sha": "d8742416ae81870e86f9df69006521f322634862",
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/lilliput/git/trees/d8742416ae81870e86f9df69006521f322634862"
          },
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/lilliput/git/commits/6ad985f1e58e5d6d281c80c962e96200dcac25c6",
          "comment_count": 0,
          "verification": {
